Fix the Windows branch of libtest's testThreadedClosureVrV().

The non-pthread branch loops over t->count, but t is only declared in
the pthread branch, so libtest (built only by `ant test`) does not
compile on Windows. The call count is the parameter n.

Upstream: not submitted
Applies-to: all environments (test library only)

--- a/libtest/ClosureTest.c
+++ b/libtest/ClosureTest.c
@@ -124,7 +124,7 @@
     pthread_join(t, NULL);
 #else
     int i;
-    for (i = 0; i < t->count; i++) {
+    for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {
         (*closure)();
     }
 #endif
